    <string name="about_story_title">Origin Story of NetPass</string>
    <string name="about_story_body">NetPass was born out of a real personal need for a trustworthy, ad-free, open-source Wi-Fi voucher scanner tailored for blind users and screen readers.\n\nIt was built from the ground up with modern native Android technologies (Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, and CameraX) to stay free and open to everyone.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_title">Strict Privacy &amp; Security Pledge</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_bullet_1">• No external servers: login traffic stays strictly between your phone and your local MikroTik router gateway.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_bullet_2">• Zero tracking and zero ads: no analytics SDKs, trackers, or hidden ad modules.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_bullet_3">• 100% on-device OCR: frames are analyzed locally in memory and never saved.</string>
    <string name="about_editions_title">Available Editions:</string>
    <string name="about_edition_full">• Full Edition (~21MB): bundles the offline ML Kit OCR model so it works anywhere without Google Play Services.</string>
    <string name="about_edition_lite">• Lite Edition (~2.7MB): minimal download size that fetches the OCR model dynamically via Google Play Services.</string>
